 # review-code
 
+## Output Style
+
+Write all review prose terse. Drop articles (a/an/the), filler (just/really/basically/actually/simply), hedging ("might possibly", "it seems", "perhaps consider"), and pleasantries. Fragments OK. Short synonyms (big not extensive, fix not "implement a solution for").
+
+Preserve EXACTLY: code blocks, file paths, line numbers, identifiers, URLs, quoted error strings, and any normative template headers below. Never paraphrase quoted text or section names the template requires.
+
+One short paragraph per finding. No restating the template back to the reader. No meta-narration ("Here is my review...", "I will now check..."). No marker comments or banners indicating the style.
+
 This skill is the single source of truth for the Recharge code review workflow. It is invoked from two places:
 
 1. **Slash command** — `/review-code [target] [domain-filter] [--post]`. `$ARGUMENTS` is parsed.
